/*!
	\page tutorial.html tutorial
	\title Bullet Hell Game Tutorial using Felgo

	\section1 Introduction

	This tutorial describes how to create a simple 2D Bullet Hell Game using Felgo.

	The tutorial will go in details on how to implement the player control and shooting mechanics,
	enemies and their attack patterns, wave spawning and scene management.

	The source code for the finished is available on \l {https://github.com/Anton3311/felgo-challenge} {GitHub}

	\section1 Assets

	The art assets used throughout this tutorial are from Kenney and are available \l {https://kenney.nl/assets/tiny-dungeon} {here} under CC0 1.0 License. This asset pack doesn't cover all of the need art assets, thus some of the missing ones were hand-drawn in the same style. All of the used art assets are available in GitHub Repository under \l {https://github.com/Anton3311/felgo-challenge/tree/main/assets/entities} {assets/entities}

	The pixel font used in the game is available on \l {https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Jersey+10?query=Jersey+10&preview.script=Latn} {Google Fonts}

	\section1 Project Setup

	Start by creating a new \b{Felgo Games} project in Qt Creator. Sepcifically we will need
	\b{New - Empty Felgo Project} template.

